1. The insurance cover must indemnify an insurance marketing firm against:
a. any error or omission or negligence on their part or on the part of their employees (including ISPs, FSEs) and
directors;
b. any loss of money or other property for which the Insurance Marketing Firm is legally liable in consequence of any
financial or fraudulent act or omission;
c. any loss of documents and costs and expenses incurred in replacing or restoring such documents;
d. dishonest or fraudulent acts or omissions by Insurance Marketing Firms' employees or former employees.
